#
# OntoUML metamodel model — the FreeRole anti-pattern (documented in the OntoUML
# anti-pattern catalogue at https://ontouml.readthedocs.io/en/latest/anti-patterns/).
#
# An anti-rigid sortal (a role) must specialize a rigid sortal (kind/subkind) to
# inherit a principle of identity. ex:Customer is a role with NO rigid ancestor, so
# it violates the discipline (and, tracing to zero Kinds, additionally trips the
# identity discipline — the faithful full lint set). The documented verdict is
# FreeRole; the native disciplines must reproduce it.

@prefix ontouml: <https://w3id.org/ontouml#> .
@prefix ex:      <https://gmeow.example/ontouml-mini/free-role/> .

ex:Customer a ontouml:Class ; ontouml:stereotype ontouml:role .
